{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "יזל מים", :translit "yizal mayim", :gloss "he shall pour water"} {:he "יגדל מלך", :translit "yigdal melekh", :gloss "a king shall be exalted"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "יזל מים", :b "יגדל מלך"}], :frame {:text "The opening phrase of Balaam's blessing — 'Water shall flow from his branches' (Numbers 24:7) — is read as a prophecy of Israelite kingship. The practice of anointing a king by a river is attested as the procedure for the king of Israel: Solomon is anointed at the Gihon spring (1 Kings 1:33-38, referenced in Horayot 12a). The flowing water symbolizes that the king's reign should be continuous and ever-increasing.", :sources ["Numbers 24:7" "1 Kings 1:33-38" "Horayot 12a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "יזל מים", :a-value 137, :b "יגדל מלך", :b-value 137, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:31:12.005439507Z", :model "glm-5.2"}